  <main_text>
    <l n="1">cato originali dici non poffint. Sed</l>
    <l n="2">debebat Profeffor controverfiarum</l>
    <l n="3">fuos difcipulos de vero controverfiæ</l>
    <l n="4">ftatu fideliter inftituere, quod cùm non</l>
    <l n="5">fecerit, ego id pro declaratione &amp; de-</l>
    <l n="6">fenfione fententiæ orthodoxæ hoc lo-</l>
    <l n="7">co faciam. Nam non tantùm Har-</l>
    <l n="8">fcherus, fed &amp; <i>Bellarminus</i> &amp; <i>Becanus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">hic fraudulenter agunt.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Obfervandum igitur, quid orthodo-</l>
    <l n="11">xi nominibus <i>peccati originalis &amp; con-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>cupiscentiæ</i> intelligant. Peccati origi-</l>
    <l n="13">nalis nomine intelligunt naturalem ho-</l>
    <l n="14">minis vitiositatem, depravationem &amp;</l>
    <l n="15">corruptionem, omnibus hominibus na-</l>
    <l n="16">turaliter ex Adamo defcendentibus in-</l>
    <l n="17">exiftentem, immiffam pofteris propter</l>
    <l n="18">reatum peccati Adami. Corruptio</l>
    <l n="19">illa partim <i>privativa</i> partim <i>pofitiva</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">eft.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Privativa</i> corruptio eft, quâ in ho-</l>
    <l n="22">mine lapfo dona tum naturalia corru-</l>
    <l n="23">pta funt, tum fupernaturalia fublata.</l>
